course: dictionary
lesson: 15801
title: Unavailable: not there to use right now
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unavailable is made of three parts: un- (meaning not), avail (meaning can be used or got), and -able (meaning can be). Put together, unavailable means not able to be got, bought or used right now.
explain: On a website you might read, «This item is currently unavailable.» The shop does not have it to sell right now, so you cannot buy it. The word currently is a clue: it may be back later.
explain: The word can also describe a person. «Mrs Patel is unavailable until Thursday, because she is away.» Here unavailable means she is not free to meet, talk or help, because she is busy or away.
explain: In a maths problem, an unavailable item is left out. «Sam has 5 pens, but 2 are unavailable, so he counts only 3.» Ask yourself: can I use it right now? If not, it is unavailable.
fact: Unavailable is an adjective, so it describes a thing or a person.
fact: Un- at the start means not, so unavailable means not available.
fact: «Available» means able to be got, bought or used, or free to help.
fact: «This item is currently unavailable» means you cannot get it right now.
fact: A person can be unavailable when they are busy or away, as in «The teacher is unavailable during the meeting.»
exercise: «This item is currently unavailable.» What does this message tell you? | It is the cheapest thing in the shop | It is free to take home today | *You cannot get or buy it right now
exercise: «The head teacher is unavailable this morning, because she is at a meeting.» What does unavailable mean here? | Lost forever | Very angry with the class | *Busy, so not free to talk
exercise: In a maths problem, an unavailable item is... | Counted twice in the total | *Left out of the total or the choices | Given to the teacher to keep
test: «The bike shop had no more helmets, so the helmets were unavailable.» What does unavailable mean? | *Could not be got right now | Painted bright blue | Free and cheap
test: Which word has the same un- meaning as unavailable? | *unhappy | happiness | happily
exam: Mum says, «The doctor is unavailable right now, so ring back later.» Why should you ring back later? | The doctor is free to talk right now | The doctor has moved to another town | *The doctor is busy and not free to talk right now
